From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cristian Papa <pcristian292@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 13:01:49 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 03/48] net: xpon: omci: put the alarm sequence number in
 content byte 32

The baseline Alarm notification of G.988 (Annex A) carries the alarm
bit map in content bytes 1-28, three bytes of zero padding and the alarm
sequence number in byte 32. The dying gasp notification wrote the
sequence number right after the bit map, in byte 29, so the OLT read a
sequence number of 0, which is reserved.

The sequence also restarts when the OLT resynchronises the alarm state:
reset it on Get all alarms and on MIB reset, not only when the OMCC
channel goes down, so the next notification is numbered 1 again.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 net/xpon/omci/agent.c | 12 +++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/net/xpon/omci/agent.c b/net/xpon/omci/agent.c
index 7acc45d..4cbc71d 100644
--- a/net/xpon/omci/agent.c
+++ b/net/xpon/omci/agent.c
@@ -149,8 +149,12 @@ static bool omci_agent_result_can_be_faked(u8 result)
 #define OMCI_ATTRIBUTE_FORMAT_TABLE		7
 
 #define OMCI_ONU_G_DYING_GASP_ALARM	7
+/*
+ * G.988 baseline Alarm notification contents: bytes 1-28 alarm bit map,
+ * bytes 29-31 zero padding, byte 32 alarm sequence number.
+ */
 #define OMCI_ALARM_BITMAP_LEN		28
-#define OMCI_ALARM_SEQUENCE_OFFSET	(8 + OMCI_ALARM_BITMAP_LEN)
+#define OMCI_ALARM_SEQUENCE_OFFSET	(8 + 31)
 
 #define OMCI_ANI_G_ENTITY_ID		0x8001
 #define OMCI_ETHERNET_SLOT		0x01
@@ -2663,6 +2667,7 @@ static int omci_agent_mib_reset_locked(struct omci_device *odev, bool all,
 
 	omci_agent_set_mib_sync_locked(agent, 0);
 	agent->upload_index = 0;
+	agent->alarm_sequence = 0;
 	omci_agent_reset_duplicate_locked(agent);
 
 	/*
@@ -4723,6 +4728,11 @@ omci_agent_build_response_locked(struct omci_device *odev,
 	case OMCI_MSG_TYPE_GET_ALL_ALARMS:
 		if (capacity < 3)
 			return -EMSGSIZE;
+		/*
+		 * Get all alarms resynchronises the OLT with the alarm state;
+		 * the next notification starts the sequence again at 1.
+		 */
+		agent->alarm_sequence = 0;
 		content[0] = OMCI_RESULT_SUCCESS;
 		put_unaligned_be16(0, content + 1);
 		*content_len = 3;
